WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.467 align:middle line:90%


00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.868 align:middle line:84%
Well, since we
are short on time,

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.637 align:middle line:84%
I'll have to move on to
chapter five on property.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.339 align:middle line:84%
But explore when
you can what he says

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.843 align:middle line:84%
about the state of war and
slavery in the Skip chapters.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.945 align:middle line:84%
We will also come back
to other subtleties,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:14.214 align:middle line:84%
like why he calls the
doctrine by everyone

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.349 align:middle line:84%
in the state of nature
has executive power

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.052 align:middle line:84%
this strange doctrine
in paragraph 13

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.520 align:middle line:84%
and, for that
matter, why there is

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.058 align:middle line:84%
no authority in the state of
nature besides each individual.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:29.429 align:middle line:84%
So what are his key
arguments on property?

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.930 align:middle line:90%
Alyssa.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.934 align:middle line:84%
One is that each of us has a
property in our own person.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.936 align:middle line:90%
That's in paragraph 27.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:37.537 align:middle line:90%
Good.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:41.341 align:middle line:84%
And later in paragraph 27, that
we make things our property

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.710 align:middle line:84%
by mixing our labor
with things from nature.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.477 align:middle line:90%
Very good.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:44.978 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.479 align:middle line:90%
I like the acorn example.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:49.549 align:middle line:84%
By picking up an
acorn, we make it ours.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.151 align:middle line:84%
I guess that applies
to fruit, too.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.952 align:middle line:90%
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:57.057 align:middle line:84%
And he says in paragraph
26 that the Earth is ours

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.159 align:middle line:84%
for the support and
comfort of our being

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.428 align:middle line:84%
and that we're given
reason to use it well.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.596 align:middle line:84%
That brings me back to
my point from before.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.765 align:middle line:84%
Someone isn't using it
well if they're rich

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.900 align:middle line:90%
and they hoard things.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.902 align:middle line:84%
Well, you can only
hoard so much.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.537 align:middle line:90%
Like, who needs 10 Ferraris?

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.072 align:middle line:90%
I do.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.206 align:middle line:90%
Ha, ha.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.707 align:middle line:90%
Ha, ha, yourself.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.176 align:middle line:84%
The point is that you cannot
hoard because your things will

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:17.944 align:middle line:90%
spoil.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:18.678 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.547 align:middle line:84%
That is why he talks
about money somewhere.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.682 align:middle line:90%
Money doesn't go bad.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.851 align:middle line:90%
Yes, in paragraph 36.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.687 align:middle line:84%
But you'll see that he
says in paragraph 31

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.223 align:middle line:84%
that everyone can take as
much as he wants from nature,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.925 align:middle line:90%
but there is a limitation.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.994 align:middle line:84%
What is that limitation that
prevents us from accumulating

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.664 align:middle line:90%
so much that things spoil?

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.934 align:middle line:84%
Well, what is also present
in nature besides things

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.569 align:middle line:90%
you can take?

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.402 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.771 align:middle line:90%
The law of reason.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.707 align:middle line:84%
It's stupid to hoard because
then you're just wasting stuff,

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.442 align:middle line:84%
and that's against
the law of reason.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:53.313 align:middle line:84%
But once there is money, you
can hoard it without spoiling.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:56.116 align:middle line:90%
So why isn't that wrong to do?

00:01:56.116 --> 00:02:00.120 align:middle line:84%
Because you put
your labor into it?

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.988 align:middle line:90%
But what if you're just lucky?

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.824 align:middle line:90%
Or what if you inherited it?

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.993 align:middle line:90%
OK if I answer this one?

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.930 align:middle line:84%
It's because someone else
put their labor into it,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:15.702 align:middle line:84%
therefore they can give
however they choose.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.436 align:middle line:90%
Excellent.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.603 align:middle line:90%
Thanks.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:20.440 align:middle line:84%
Do you recall how much
Locke says labor increases

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.643 align:middle line:90%
the value of what is in nature?

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.345 align:middle line:90%
100 times in paragraph 40.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.747 align:middle line:90%
1,000 times in paragraph 43.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.750 align:middle line:84%
Both 10 and 100 times
in paragraph 37.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.852 align:middle line:84%
And since we mentioned
paragraph 40,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.687 align:middle line:84%
we should point out
his famous statement

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.222 align:middle line:90%
in the subsequent one.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.025 align:middle line:84%
A king of a large and
fruitful territory in America

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.929 align:middle line:84%
feeds, lodges, and is clad worse
than a day laborer in England.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.531 align:middle line:84%
So whatever the
factor of increase is,

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:48.868 align:middle line:84%
the point is not just that
labor is almost all the value

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.804 align:middle line:84%
in property but that
by protecting property

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.440 align:middle line:84%
we will all benefit
with many good things.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.975 align:middle line:90%
Yes, like this university.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.310 align:middle line:90%
[CHUCKLES]

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.211 align:middle line:90%
Exactly.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.880 align:middle line:84%
I still don't think it's fair
that some people have so much

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.549 align:middle line:90%
more than others.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.651 align:middle line:90%
But we all benefit.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.719 align:middle line:84%
Besides, if it weren't
for this system,

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.189 align:middle line:84%
you wouldn't even be able
to get that broken-down Kia

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.423 align:middle line:90%
that you dream of.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:10.924 align:middle line:90%
Oh.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:11.658 align:middle line:90%
Ha, ha.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:14.761 align:middle line:90%
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.130 align:middle line:84%
But even if the pie
gets bigger and bigger,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.898 align:middle line:84%
some people will
still control others

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.500 align:middle line:84%
because they have
a bigger piece,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.970 align:middle line:90%
making those people unhappy.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.172 align:middle line:90%
Or do you mean less free?

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:30.109 align:middle line:84%
If so, it seems that AI doesn't
solve the problem at all.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.645 align:middle line:84%
Of course, some people
do think that it can,

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.581 align:middle line:84%
that mathematization
of all things

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.517 align:middle line:84%
can lead to a sort
of techno utopia.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.485 align:middle line:90%
Locke is giving us a choice.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:43.089 align:middle line:84%
We can be controlled by
algorithms designed by smart

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:46.893 align:middle line:84%
but unworldly people working
long hours in some basement--

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.162 align:middle line:90%
or let's call it a cave--

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.798 align:middle line:84%
or we can be allowed
our own choice.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:53.766 align:middle line:84%
Of course, that choice
should be the product

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.970 align:middle line:84%
of thoughtful reflection,
particularly on our own biases.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:01.140 align:middle line:84%
But AI could give more
freedom, couldn't it?

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.308 align:middle line:90%
I see what you're saying.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.944 align:middle line:84%
Certainly, it can bring
benefits in health care

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:08.348 align:middle line:84%
and transportation and make
many things more efficient.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.817 align:middle line:84%
But intrinsically it
can't solve the problem

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.553 align:middle line:90%
of bias even in itself.

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.255 align:middle line:90%
Actually, it's even worse.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.257 align:middle line:84%
Those who develop and
therefore control AI

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:21.628 align:middle line:84%
will build AI systems biased
for their own benefit.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:22.128 align:middle line:90%
Hmm.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.129 align:middle line:90%
Hmm.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.531 align:middle line:84%
Having said that, I
realized that we somehow

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.568 align:middle line:84%
seem to have gotten
distracted from understanding

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:33.139 align:middle line:84%
how natural right can help
us to address bias in AI.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:36.376 align:middle line:84%
And we only have a few
minutes of class left.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.345 align:middle line:84%
I was wondering when you
were going to realize that.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.248 align:middle line:84%
Well, you convinced
us that all AI systems

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.750 align:middle line:84%
will be biased in
some dimensions

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.685 align:middle line:90%
no matter what you do.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:49.222 align:middle line:84%
But then you also
convinced us that property

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.224 align:middle line:90%
should be respected.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:54.294 align:middle line:90%
So, what do we do about bias?

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:54.794 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.963 align:middle line:84%
And how should we
punish people who write

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.165 align:middle line:90%
unacceptably biased AI systems?

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:03.636 align:middle line:84%
Or reward them for making
acceptably biased AI systems.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.271 align:middle line:90%
I mean unbiased AI systems.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.739 align:middle line:90%
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:07.240 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.908 align:middle line:84%
We can't reward
or punish people,

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.311 align:middle line:90%
according to Locke's system.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.980 align:middle line:84%
On the contrary,
we can reward them

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.115 align:middle line:84%
by buying their
products if we like them

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.284 align:middle line:84%
or punish them by not
buying their products

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.719 align:middle line:90%
if we don't like them.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.954 align:middle line:90%
So transparency is the key?

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:25.491 align:middle line:84%
Yes, if people are willing
to pay for transparency.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.528 align:middle line:84%
You see, the law of
nature addresses that too.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.496 align:middle line:84%
And in most
contemporary approaches,

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.432 align:middle line:84%
there is an
assumption, one which

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:34.367 align:middle line:84%
we have been
addressing today too,

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:37.170 align:middle line:84%
that bias is bad and
should be eradicated

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.539 align:middle line:90%
by technical mathematical means.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:42.842 align:middle line:84%
We now understand that a deeper
reflection on the law of nature

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.712 align:middle line:84%
and the law of reason is
needed, but we engineers

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.514 align:middle line:84%
needed to see the limitations
of the mathematical or computer

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.850 align:middle line:84%
science approach
first before we turn

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.452 align:middle line:90%
to a broader or deeper one.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:52.952 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:56.489 align:middle line:84%
I think I understand
this now, but it still

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.391 align:middle line:90%
hasn't changed one thing.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.659 align:middle line:90%
I want a Ferrari.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.694 align:middle line:90%
[SCOFFING, CHUCKLING]

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:06.032 align:middle line:84%
The point is under the Lockean
system we are all better off--

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.633 align:middle line:90%
happier, we could say--

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.969 align:middle line:84%
because algorithms
with unacceptable

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:13.406 align:middle line:84%
bias will go away because
no one will buy them.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.341 align:middle line:90%
You're starting to understand.